SWEET AKS: keybagd's two-phase passcode change, committed at selector 5 (2324)

With 2323 the kernel stores the right code at selector 15, and keybagd still
reports failure. KBChangeSystemNonSeSecret (keybagd 0x10001ce48; MobileKeyBag
0x1cb461ce8 is the same code) takes the "two" phase whenever lock-state bit 22,
keybag_state_from_xart, is clear, which it is on any phone without a SEP. It then
puts 4 in selector 15's scalar 1 and expects a temporary bag handle in scalar
output 0, saves that bag (selector 3), makes it the system bag (selector 5,
aks_set_system_with_opts {temp, device, new, len, acm}), runs the epilogue (105)
and unloads it (selector 4). 2321 returned no handle, so keybagd logged "temp
handle is invalid: 0" after the code was already stored.

- Selector 15 with scalar 1 bit 0x4 runs every 2321 and 2323 check in the same
  order, then only stages: the copied or resolved codes, the owner (the user
  client) and a fresh temporary handle (1..0x7fffffff, never 0 or -1), returned
  in scalar output 0. Nothing is hashed, counted or written.
- Selector 3 on the staged handle answers "SWEET", the KeyBagKeys bytes the root
  image's systembag.kb already holds. Every other handle stays Unsupported.
- Selector 5 on the staged handle, from the same client, is the commit: the
  entitlement, the device bag, the same kind of code, the same new code as
  staged, the state known, then pc_do() exactly as 2321's selector 15 ran it,
  with the live state decided at commit. A wrong old code is counted there, by
  the core, before it is hashed. The stage is consumed whatever the outcome.
- Selector 4 on the staged handle, clientClose and the next stage wipe it.
- Selector 15 without the bit (MobileKeyBag in process), selector 5 on any other
  handle, the stub mode and the lock state are unchanged. Bit 22 is never set.

A crash or reboot between 15 and 5 leaves the old code: nothing reaches the disk
before the commit.

Needs 2321, 2322 and 2323. Security code: plans/passcode/audit-brief-2phase.md is
the audit brief, and no image should boot until that audit is a GO.

Check: python3 -I plans/passcode/tools/check-2phase.py XNU_DIR (35 checks, 19 negative controls)
       python3 -I plans/passcode/tools/check-lock.py XNU_DIR (2321/2322)
Apply: git apply -p1 in the kernel tree, after 2321, 2322 and 2323.
